   "evidence": "Mathlib splits on the *written* LHS: `Complex.I_re : I.re = 0` (Mathlib/Basic/Complex/Basic.lean:244) and `Complex.I_im` (line 248) are instance-first because the LHS is `I.re`; `normSq_I` (line 552), `arg_I`, `norm_I`, `conj_I` are function-first because the LHS is `normSq I`. Here every statement is written `proton.neutronNumber = 0`, `proton.massNumber = 1`, i.e. uniformly dot form, so all fifteen should take the same order. Rubric: \"Check adjacent declarations first: consistency beats a theoretically better name.\"",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Nuclei/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Rename the five to `proton_neutronNumber`, `neutron_neutronNumber`, `deuteron_neutronNumber`, `carbon12_neutronNumber`, `lead208_neutronNumber`, matching the adjacent block. (The `isIsoscalar_<nucleus>` lemmas are correct as-is under the predicate-as-prefix rule and should not change.)",
